    pr_ref:  # 98f3
    description: "AGENTS.md:82 (always-loaded governance text) documents an invocation that exits 2:\n\n    scripts/tracker show <ID> --json      # usage error, exit 2\n\nThe working form puts the global flag before the subcommand:\n\n    scripts/tracker --json show <ID>\n\nWHY IT COSTS MORE THAN A TYPO. Both of the two ways to get this wrong --\nwrong flag position, and running the CLI from outside the repo root -- write\ntheir diagnostic to STDERR and produce nothing on STDOUT. Any verification\nloop that pipes stdout to a JSON parser and discards stderr therefore renders\n\"I invoked the CLI wrong\" and \"that item does not exist\" IDENTICALLY. Observed\ntwice in two consecutive sessions: a 13-ID and a 42-ID status sweep both\nreturned a full column of false UNRESOLVED. This is LIVE.md rule 5 (\"a zero and\na missing input must not look the same\") reproduced by the instrument the rule\nwas written about.\n\nTWO PARTS, SEPARABLE:\n\n(a) DOC. Correct AGENTS.md:82 to the working form. Governance file, so it\n    needs the owner's standing governance pre-approval or an explicit ack.\n    One line.\n\n(b) STRUCTURAL, and the part that actually stops the recurrence. Make the\n    failure loud on the STDOUT side, so a stdout-only consumer cannot read a\n    usage error as an absent item. Options, cheapest first:\n      - accept the trailing --json form as an alias (argparse: add --json to\n        the subparsers as well as the top-level parser), which removes the\n        flag-position hazard entirely rather than documenting around it;\n      - and/or emit a JSON error object on stdout with a nonzero exit when\n        --json is in effect, so a parser sees {\"error\": ...} not empty input.\n    The alias is the smaller change and kills the larger share of the hazard;\n    the wrong-cwd case still exits nonzero with empty stdout and would need the\n    second option.\n\nDISCOVERED: 2026-09-10, verifying LIVE.md's roster claims at session start.\nNOT a blocker for any arc cell -- filed so it is not relearned a third time."  # 98f3
    fields: {}  # 98f3
